# Example ReRDMFT input file: LiH, 6-31G, CASSCF with the 4-component min-max stage.
#
# CASSCF first optimizes the orbitals over the positive-energy spinors only (no-pair); CASSCF_4C_NEG TRUE then
# continues with rotations that also mix the occupied positive-energy spinors with the negative-energy ones, driven by ADAM
# (always: the CAS model has no Hessian-vector product for NEO), and the CI is re-solved.
# Validation: 4 electrons in 4 spinors (CASSCF_ELECTRONS 4, CASSCF_SPINORS 4) is a single determinant, so the min-max energy must equal the Dirac-Hartree-Fock one
# (checked at SPEED_OF_LIGHT 20 -- where the electron-positron relaxation is 1.5e-6 Ha -- to 1e-10 Ha). The core-Hamiltonian start
# makes the no-pair stage differ from the DHF orbitals.
NELEC 4
BASIS lih-6-31g.gbs
C4_SPINOR TRUE
CASSCF TRUE
CASSCF_INIT CORE
CASSCF_ELECTRONS 4
CASSCF_SPINORS 4
CASSCF_4C_NEG TRUE
SPEED_OF_LIGHT 20
USE_RI FALSE

GEOMETRY
Li  0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.000000   1.594900
END
